  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "One of the most noticeable signs of reaching the **\"intermediate plateau\"** in English is relying on the modifier **\"very\"** to intensify everyday adjectives."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "While saying *\"very big\"*, *\"very good\"*, or *\"very bad\"* is grammatically correct and understandable, overusing *\"very\"* makes your speech and writing sound repetitive. Transitioning to stronger, more expressive single-word adjectives immediately makes your English sound more natural, sophisticated, and precise."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Here are 50 of the most common *\"very...\"* combinations along with their natural, powerful alternatives."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "50 Better Alternatives to \"Very + Adjective\""
